{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Elohim remembered, etc.</b> The verse informs that even though her remembrance had already ascended before Him, she still needed prayer, as it says: ״וַיִּשְׁמַע אֵלֶיהָ״ etc." "<b>Further,</b> the verse makes known that HaShem remembers His devout ones even without their crying out to Him; therefore it says <b>וַיִּזְכֹּר</b> etc., and afterward <b>וַיִּשְׁמַע</b> etc. — to say that before she prayed, her remembrance had already ascended before Him, blessed be He."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:04.209341957Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}